---
/**
 * Blog hub: public essays and field notes that articulate Identity Engineering
 * against classical theories and emerging practice.
 */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';

const posts = [
	{
		href: '/blog/analogy-isomorphy-and-the-engineering-stance',
		date: 'August 2026',
		readTime: '12 min',
		title: 'Analogy, Isomorphy, and the Engineering Stance',
		excerpt:
			'Why Identity Engineering treats physics mappings as productive analogy and long-term isomorphy work, not as settled isomorphism. The operational proof is the OS and measurable improvement of geometry.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/account-not-identity',
		date: 'August 2026',
		readTime: '10 min',
		title: 'Account ≠ Identity',
		excerpt:
			'An IE Account is auth and plan on the product. Geometry lives only on Identities. Harnesses bind to an Identity, never to an anonymous account mode.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/one-space-degrees-of-freedom-and-membrane',
		date: 'August 2026',
		readTime: '12 min',
		title: 'One Space: Degrees of Freedom and Membrane',
		excerpt:
			'Physics names the arena of degrees of freedom. Biology names the membrane of the form that lives in that arena. They are two scientific cuts of one Space, not two hosts and not two ontologies.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/creation-as-first-access-agreement',
		date: 'August 2026',
		readTime: '13 min',
		title: 'Creation as First Access Agreement',
		excerpt:
			'Creating an Identity is two things at once: factual lineage and a default jurisdiction package. Parent-Child is not ownership of the Child Stem. It is the first Access Agreement the framework makes explicit.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/identifying-opportunities-higher-order-liberation',
		date: 'August 2026',
		readTime: '12 min',
		title: 'Identifying Opportunities as Higher-Order Liberation',
		excerpt:
			'When competing high-Mass stems steal energy from each other, the resolution is not fewer identities. It is the identification of a new identity whose curvature liberates both. That act is the core of Identity Engineering on the collective layer.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/ownership-as-relative-jurisdiction',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '14 min',
		title: 'Ownership as Relative Jurisdiction',
		excerpt:
			'Ownership is not absolute possession. It is the relative, gradual distribution of degrees of freedom (Access and Jurisdiction) with respect to a thing. The only durable claim is over the Identity Stem.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/causal-entropy-as-design-telos',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '14 min',
		title: 'Causal Entropy as Design Telos',
		excerpt:
			'Multi-source scientific grounding for the Vision Gradient. Why maximizing future freedom of action is a normative design goal, not a derived physical law.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/particles-of-identity',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '15 min',
		title: 'Particles of Identity',
		excerpt:
			'Space as the order of relative positions. Particles as the first bound configurations. Why degrees of freedom cohere before Time can draw the Stem.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/the-tension-field-spannung-in-identity-engineering',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '18 min',
		title: 'The Tension Field: Spannung as the Central Dynamic of Identity Engineering',
		excerpt:
			'The geometric primitives are not the deepest layer. The real core is a single continuous phenomenon running through all of them: the multidimensional tension field in which every identity exists and acts.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/energy-forms-of-identity',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '16 min',
		title: 'Energy Forms of Identity',
		excerpt:
			'Mass-Energy, Gravitation and Causal Entropy are powerful. But what about Electromagnetism, Kinetics, and the Strong Force? A systematic gap analysis with concrete extension proposals.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/identity-as-trajectory',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '16 min',
		title: 'Identity as Trajectory',
		excerpt:
			'From snapshot sameness to a causal Worldline that balances past differential and future freedom. The mathematical core of Sameness-as-Trajectory and the Identity Stem force balance.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/organizational-identity-engineering',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '14 min',
		title: 'Organizational Identity Engineering: Rebuilding Coherent Order in Complex Collective Systems',
		excerpt:
			'A geometric perspective on why large organizations drift into incoherence, and how aligned Real Mass rebuilds value-creating order.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/regulatory-geometry-eu-ai-act',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '18 min',
		title: 'The Tension Continuum: High-Dimensional Dynamics and Resonance in Identity Engineering',
		excerpt:
			'From regulatory geometry to a high-dimensional tension field: a dynamics-first extension of Identity Engineering for human-AI co-identity.',
	},
	{
		href: '/blog/identity-engineering-vs-classical-identity-theories',
		date: 'July 2026',
		readTime: '12 min',
		title: 'Identity Engineering vs. Classical Identity Theories',
		excerpt:
			'Locke, Hume, Erikson: and the leap from retrospective maps to a physics-informed, designable geometry of self.',
	},
];
---

<Layout title="Blog | Identity Engineering">
	<main class="min-h-screen">
		<section class="border-b border-white/10 px-6 pt-28 pb-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl">
				<div class="mb-4 text-sm uppercase tracking-[4px] text-white/40">Blog</div>
				<h1 class="text-5xl font-bold tracking-tighter text-white md:text-6xl leading-[0.95]">
					Open Thought
				</h1>
				<p class="mt-6 max-w-2xl text-xl font-light leading-relaxed text-white/50">
					The trajectory of Identity Engineering itself becomes transparent through thinking openly about the biggest questions that position the framework, deepen its historical anchors, and make the engineering leap legible.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="px-6 py-16">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-8">
				{
					posts.map((post) => (
						<a
							href={post.href}
							class="group block border-l border-white/15 pl-6 transition-colors hover:border-white/40"
						>
							<div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-x-3 gap-y-1 text-sm text-white/40">
								<span>{post.date}</span>
								<span aria-hidden="true">·</span>
								<span>{post.readTime} read</span>
							</div>
							<h2 class="mt-2 text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight text-white transition group-hover:text-white/90 md:text-3xl">
								{post.title}
								<span class="ml-2 inline-block text-white/30 transition group-hover:translate-x-0.5 group-hover:text-white/60">
									→
								</span>
							</h2>
							<p class="mt-3 text-lg leading-relaxed text-white/55">{post.excerpt}</p>
						</a>
					))
				}
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="border-t border-white/10 px-6 py-14">
			<div class="mx-auto max-w-3xl text-sm text-white/45">
				<p>
					Historical deep-dives live in <a href="/foundations" class="text-white/70 underline decoration-white/25 underline-offset-4 transition hover:text-white hover:decoration-white/50">Foundations</a>. These are living reference pages for the anchors named in these essays.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>
	</main>
</Layout>
